I think the big distinction is

247
00:14:18,881 --> 00:14:20,800
that when someone wants a driver,

248
00:14:20,801 --> 00:14:23,380
a driver is someone who delivers a pizza.

249
00:14:23,381 --> 00:14:25,280
A true professional chauffeur

250
00:14:25,281 --> 00:14:27,780
is undoubtedly going to be drug tested,

251
00:14:27,781 --> 00:14:30,280
he was background checked before he was hired,

252
00:14:30,281 --> 00:14:32,680
and is a person that can be trusted.

253
00:14:32,681 --> 00:14:34,620
You have to know how to accelerate

254
00:14:34,621 --> 00:14:36,120
so that the person in the back

255
00:14:36,121 --> 00:14:37,260
could literally be standing there

256
00:14:37,261 --> 00:14:39,860
water in their hand and not spill any of the water.

257
00:14:42,860 --> 00:14:46,260
Maybe it's a celebrity or a sports team owner.

258
00:14:46,360 --> 00:14:49,000
They expect a five-star service.

259
00:14:49,100 --> 00:14:51,000
Sometimes they're very demanding and they need it.

260
00:14:51,100 --> 00:14:54,220
You know, they really need it now, now, now.

261
00:14:54,320 --> 00:14:58,420
In the dawn of the for hire era, the teens and 20s,

262
00:14:58,520 --> 00:15:01,420
the demand for service was just as great.

263
00:15:01,520 --> 00:15:04,460
J.P. Carey, a Grand Central Station barber,

264
00:15:04,461 --> 00:15:09,660
seized the opportunity to start a for-hire limousine business.

265
00:15:09,661 --> 00:15:11,800
From his vantage point in the train station,

266
00:15:11,801 --> 00:15:14,300
Carey saw the need for out-of-town business people

267
00:15:14,301 --> 00:15:17,200
and tourists to hire stylish transportation

268
00:15:17,201 --> 00:15:19,800
around Manhattan.

269
00:15:19,801 --> 00:15:22,620
He launched the first successful service in the US

270
00:15:22,621 --> 00:15:25,220
in 1921 in New York City.

271
00:15:25,221 --> 00:15:29,120
His company, the Grand Central Packard Renting Corporation,

272
00:15:29,121 --> 00:15:32,620
featured some of the best limousines of the day,

273
00:15:32,621 --> 00:15:36,460
Packards and Cadillacs. Tightened purse strings during

274
00:15:36,461 --> 00:15:39,460
the Depression forced limousine owners to sell their cars to

275
00:15:39,461 --> 00:15:43,460
carry, strengthening his business. People would call him

276
00:15:43,461 --> 00:15:47,220
up and say, hey, I want you to buy my car, hire my chauffeur,

277
00:15:47,221 --> 00:15:50,980
and I'll hire you whenever I want him.

278
00:15:50,981 --> 00:15:53,660
So the for-hired limousine is actually benefited by an

279
00:15:53,661 --> 00:15:56,420
economic downturn at this point, because people can't keep him

280
00:15:56,421 --> 00:15:59,780
for themselves, so they hire his on a part-time basis.

281
00:15:59,781 --> 00:16:02,380
This economic downturn put the nail on the

282
00:16:02,381 --> 00:16:07,180
of the elite custom bodybuilding companies like Brewster, Brun,

283
00:16:07,181 --> 00:16:10,180
and Willoughby. Most either went out of business

284
00:16:10,181 --> 00:16:13,680
or survived the Depression in name only as a division of a

285
00:16:13,681 --> 00:16:17,180
