00:19:49,120 --> 00:19:52,280
and stretched 100 inches.

352
00:19:52,380 --> 00:19:53,660
Cut down the middle?

353
00:19:53,661 --> 00:19:57,020
That's no way to treat a luxury automobile, but it is the first

354
00:19:57,021 --> 00:20:00,860
step in making a stretch. Most of the conversion from sedan

355
00:20:00,861 --> 00:20:05,660
to stretch is done by hand, just as it was a century ago when

356
00:20:05,661 --> 00:20:11,260
the first limousines were introduced to wealthy customers.

357
00:20:11,261 --> 00:20:14,700
This target group, which was used to comfort, was not about to

358
00:20:14,701 --> 00:20:19,260
end up behind the wheel of a Model T. Like the ride in early

359
00:20:19,261 --> 00:20:23,100
automobiles, the transition from luxury horse-drawn carriages to

360
00:20:23,101 --> 00:20:26,940
to limousines was not smooth.

361
00:20:26,941 --> 00:20:29,800
An automobile could travel faster than a horse,

362
00:20:29,801 --> 00:20:33,500
but would have to be heavy to withstand the stress.

363
00:20:33,501 --> 00:20:35,340
In addition, discerning customers

364
00:20:35,341 --> 00:20:38,000
had no intention of scrimping on luxury,

365
00:20:38,001 --> 00:20:39,780
and this meant added weight.

366
00:20:39,781 --> 00:20:42,240
Engines simply couldn't keep up.

367
00:20:42,241 --> 00:20:46,720
You couldn't have a full, enclosed, fully luxurious

368
00:20:46,721 --> 00:20:52,140
carriage pulled by a motor that only put out 10, 15 horsepower.

369
00:20:52,141 --> 00:20:55,900
This limitation hindered the limousine's acceptance.

370
00:20:55,901 --> 00:20:58,940
It would take two innovations to propel the limousine past the

371
00:20:58,941 --> 00:21:01,880
horse-drawn carriage, the development of the all-steel

372
00:21:01,881 --> 00:21:06,780
body in 1912, bringing strength without added weight,

373
00:21:06,781 --> 00:21:09,780
and the greater engine capacity resulting from the industrial

374
00:21:09,781 --> 00:21:13,380
surge of World War I. But the public's low opinion

375
00:21:13,381 --> 00:21:17,980
of automobiles, they were seen as noisy and dirty, remained a

376
00:21:17,981 --> 00:21:20,480
a greater obstacle for the limousine than technical

377
00:21:20,481 --> 00:21:22,980
considerations.

378
00:21:22,981 --> 00:21:25,720
Despite owning two Pierce Arrow limousines,

379
00:21:25,721 --> 00:21:30,920
President Taft rode to his 1909 inauguration in a carriage.

380
00:21:30,921 --> 00:21:33,320
However, while President, his love of motoring

381
00:21:33,321 --> 00:21:36,240
popularized automobiles and brought acceptance

382
00:21:36,241 --> 00:21:38,140
to the limousine.

383
00:21:38,141 --> 00:21:42,140
By 1921, President Warren Harding rode in an automobile

384
00:21:42,141 --> 00:21:45,840
from the Capitol to the White House on Inauguration Day,

385
00:21:45,841 --> 00:21:49,840
in the classic era of the custom coach-built limousine.

386
00:21:49,841 --> 00:21:54,640
The coach-built car is a car that is sent to a third party

387
00:21:54,641 --> 00:21:57,280
