388
00:21:57,281 --> 00:21:59,680
They take the factory car, which is the chassis.

389
00:21:59,681 --> 00:22:02,080
The chassis looks like an engine, the wheels,

390
00:22:02,081 --> 00:22:04,400
and the transmission all the way down the middle.

391
00:22:04,401 --> 00:22:07,600
And then from the front seats on back,

392
00:22:07,601 --> 00:22:10,000
someone else builds the rest of it.

393
00:22:10,001 --> 00:22:11,640
There were rare exceptions,

394
00:22:11,641 --> 00:22:14,400
like the Pierce-Hero Company in Buffalo, New York,

395
00:22:14,401 --> 00:22:17,040
that succeeded in making both a high-quality chassis

396
00:22:17,041 --> 00:22:18,940
and coach.

397
00:22:18,941 --> 00:22:21,840
Although this approach made for beautiful limousines,

398
00:22:21,841 --> 00:22:25,840
it wasn't the most durable business model.

399
00:22:25,841 --> 00:22:29,540
In fact, innovators rarely stayed in business long,

400
00:22:29,541 --> 00:22:32,560
and such was the fate of Skip Lehman and Robert Peterson.

401
00:22:32,561 --> 00:22:36,260
In 1963, inspired by the quality of the Lincoln Continental

402
00:22:36,261 --> 00:22:39,060
of the early 60s, they cut Lehman's Lincoln in half

